All done. Implementation details:

**`configuration.go`** — `Source` type, `Config` struct, and `Load` function that reads `HELIOS_PORT`, `HELIOS_NAME`, `HELIOS_DEBUG` with defaults (8080, `"helios"`, `false`). Parse errors propagate wrapped via `fmt.Errorf("…: %w", err)` so `errors.As`/`errors.AsType` can reach the underlying `*strconv.NumError`.

**`cmd/configprint/main.go`** — wraps `os.Getenv` as a `Source` (returning `""`/`false` for missing keys), loads config, prints `port=%d name=%s debug=%t`.

**`configuration_test.go`** — 10 tests covering:
- All defaults
- Custom values
- `Debug=false` variants (`"false"`, `"0"`, `"FALSE"`, `"f"`)
- Port out of range (0, -1, 65536, 99999)
- Port bad syntax with `errors.AsType[*strconv.NumError]` assertion
- Empty `HELIOS_NAME` error
- Bad `HELIOS_DEBUG` syntax
- All-missing (equals default struct)
- Partial override (only `HELIOS_NAME` set)

`go build ./...` ✓ `go vet ./...` ✓ `go test ./...` ✓ `bash ./check.sh` exit 0 ✓
